hadiths[73]{hadithnumber,text}:
"10399","Abu Bakrah radiya Allahu anhu reported: The Prophet of Allah ﷺ passed by a man prostrating while on his way to prayer. He completed the prayer and returned to find him still prostrating. The Prophet ﷺ stood and said: > **""Who will kill this man?""** A man rose, bared his arms, drew his sword and brandished it, then said, O Prophet of Allah, may my father and mother be ransom for you, how can I kill a prostrating man who testifies that none is worthy of worship but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. The Prophet ﷺ again said: > **""Who will kill this man?""** Another man rose and said, I will. He bared his forearms, drew his sword and brandished it until his hand trembled, then said, O Prophet of Allah, how can I kill a prostrating man who testifies that none is worthy of worship but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, had you killed him it would have been the first fitnah and the last.""**"
"10400","Abu Sa'id al-Khudri radiya Allahu anhu reported: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq radiya Allahu anhu came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, O Messenger of Allah, I passed by such-and-such a valley and saw a humble man of fine appearance praying. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: > **""Go and kill him.""** Abu Bakr went to him, saw him in that state, disliked killing him, and returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said to Umar radiya Allahu anhu: > **""Go and kill him.""** Umar went, saw him as Abu Bakr had seen him, and returned saying, O Messenger of Allah, I saw him praying humbly and disliked killing him. He said: > **""O Ali, go and kill him.""** Ali radiya Allahu anhu went but did not find him, and returned saying, O Messenger of Allah, I did not see him. The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""This man and his companions recite the Quran but it does not pass their throats. They pass through the religion as the arrow passes through the target, then never return to it until the arrow returns to its notch. Kill them; they are the worst of creation.""**"
"10401","Anas ibn Malik radiya Allahu anhu reported: In the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ there was a man who went on expedition with him. On return he would dismount, head for the mosque of the Messenger, pray at length, until the Companions thought him superior to them. One day he passed while the Messenger ﷺ sat among his Companions. A Companion said, O Messenger of Allah, there is that man. The Prophet ﷺ either sent for him or he came himself. When the Messenger ﷺ saw him approaching he said: > **""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, between his eyes is a mark of Satan.""** When he stopped at the gathering the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: > **""Did you say to yourself when you stopped at the gathering, there is none among the people better than me?""** He said, Yes. Then he left for a corner of the mosque, drew a line with his foot, straightened his heels and stood praying. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Which of you will rise to this man and kill him?""** Abu Bakr rose. The Messenger ﷺ asked: > **""Did you kill the man?""** He said, I found him praying and feared him. The Messenger ﷺ said: > **""Which of you will rise to this man and kill him?""** Umar said, I will. He took the sword, found him praying, and returned. The Messenger ﷺ asked Umar: > **""Did you kill the man?""** He said, O Messenger of Allah, I found him praying and feared him. The Messenger ﷺ said: > **""Which of you will rise to this man and kill him?""** Ali said, I will. The Messenger ﷺ said: > **""You, if you find him.""** Ali went and did not find him. The Messenger ﷺ asked: > **""Did you kill the man?""** He said, I do not know which way he went in the land. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""This is the first generation to emerge in my ummah. Had you killed him — or had he been killed — no two in my ummah would have differed. Banu Isra'il split into seventy-one sects, and this ummah will split into seventy-two sects, all in the Fire but one.""** They asked, O Prophet of Allah, which sect is that. He said: > **""The Jama'ah.""** Yazid al-Raqashi asked Anas, O Abu Hamzah, where is the Jama'ah. He said, With your rulers, with your rulers."
"10402","Anas ibn Malik radiya Allahu anhu reported: In the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ there was a man whose devotion and striving impressed us. We mentioned him by name to the Messenger ﷺ but he did not know him; we described him but he did not know him. While we spoke, the man appeared. We said, there he is. He said: > **""You tell me of a man on whose face is a mark of Satan.""** He came, stopped before them without greeting. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: > **""I adjure you by Allah, did you say when you stopped at the gathering, there is none among the people better than me?""** He said, O Allah, yes. Then he entered to pray. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Who will kill the man?""** Abu Bakr said, I will. He entered, found him standing in prayer, and said, Glory be to Allah, shall I kill a praying man when the Messenger ﷺ forbade killing those who pray. He came out. The Messenger said: > **""What did you do?""** He said, I disliked killing him while praying, and you forbade killing those who pray. Umar said, I will. He entered, found him with face lowered in prostration, and said to himself, Abu Bakr is better than me, and came out. The Messenger ﷺ said: > **""What happened?""** He said, I found him with face lowered and disliked killing him. He said: > **""Who will kill the man?""** Ali said, I will. He said: > **""You, if you reach him.""** Ali entered and found he had left, and returned to the Messenger ﷺ. He said: > **""What happened?""** He said, I did not find him. He said: > **""Had he been killed, no two men in my ummah would have differed; he would have been the first of them and the last.""** Musa heard Muhammad ibn Ka'b say, he is the one Ali killed, Dhu al-Thudayyah."
"10403","Jabir radiya Allahu anhu reported: A man passed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They spoke of him and praised him. He said: > **""Who will kill him?""** Abu Bakr said, I will. He went, found him praying within a line he had drawn for himself, saw that state, returned and did not kill him. The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Who will kill him?""** Umar said, I will. He went, saw him standing in prayer in his line, returned and did not kill him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Who is for him — or, who will kill him?""** Ali said, I will. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""You, though I do not think you will reach him.""** He set out and found he had gone."
"10404","Abu Bakrah radiya Allahu anhu reported: Dinars were brought to the Prophet ﷺ. He took handful after handful, then looked to his right as if consulting someone about whom to give to. A black man, shaven-headed, wearing two white garments, with a mark of prostration between his eyes, said, You have not been just in division. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ grew angry and said: > **""Who will be just to you after me?""** They said, O Messenger of Allah, shall we not kill him. He said: > **""No.""** Then he said to his Companions: > **""This man and his companions pass through the religion as the arrow passes through the target; they hold nothing of Islam.""**"
"10405","Miqsam, freedman of Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, reported: I and Talid ibn Kilab al-Laythi went to Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As radiya Allahu anhuma while he circumambulated the House with sandals in hand. We asked, Were you with the Messenger ﷺ when the Tamimi spoke to him on the day of Hunayn. He said, Yes. A man of Banu Tamim called Dhu al-Khuwaysirah came, stood before the Messenger ﷺ while he distributed to people, and said, O Muhammad, I have seen what you did today. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Yes, and how did it seem to you?""** He said, I do not see you were just. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ grew angry then said: > **""Woe to you, if justice is not with me, with whom is it?""** Umar ibn al-Khattab radiya Allahu anhu said, O Messenger of Allah, shall we not kill him. He said: > **""No, leave him. He has followers who delve deep into religion until they exit it as the arrow exits the target. One looks at the head and finds nothing, then at the shaft and finds nothing, then at the notch and finds nothing but dung and blood.""**"
"10406","Shahr ibn Hawshab reported: When allegiance to Yazid ibn Mu'awiyah reached us I came to Syria. I was told of a station where Nawf spoke, so I came. A man wrapped in a cloak arrived, people crowded, and he was Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As radiya Allahu anhuma. When Nawf saw him he stopped speaking. Abdullah ibn Amr said, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""People from my ummah will emerge from the east, reciting the Quran but it will not pass their throats. Every time a generation of them emerges it is cut off, every time a generation of them emerges it is cut off.""** He counted it more than ten times: > **""Every time a generation of them emerges it is cut off, until the Dajjal emerges among their remnant.""**"
"10407","Uqbah ibn Wassaj reported: A friend narrated to me about Abdullah ibn Amr concerning the Khawarij. I performed Hajj and met Abdullah ibn Amr, saying, You remain of the Companions of the Messenger ﷺ and Allah gave you knowledge; people revile their rulers and testify to their misguidance. He said, Upon them is the curse of Allah, the angels and all people. A vessel of gold or silver was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he divided it among his Companions. A desert man stood and said, O Muhammad, if Allah commanded you to be just, you were not just. He said: > **""Woe to you, who will be just to you after me?""** When he turned away the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""In my ummah are likenesses of this man. They recite the Quran but it does not pass their throats. If they rebel, kill them, then if they rebel, kill them.""** He said that three times."
"10408","Sharik ibn Shihab reported: I wished to meet a Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to narrate to me about the Khawarij. I met Abu Barzah radiya Allahu anhu on the day of Arafah among his companions and said, O Abu Barzah, narrate what you heard the Messenger ﷺ say about the Khawarij. He said, I narrate what my ears heard and my eyes saw. Dinars were brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for division. With him was a black man, shaven hair, in two white garments, with a prostration mark between his eyes. He approached the Messenger ﷺ from the front but he gave him nothing, from the right but he gave him nothing, then from behind but he gave him nothing. He said, By Allah, O Muhammad, you have not been just in division today. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ grew severely angry then said: > **""By Allah, you will find none after me more just to you than me.""** He said it three times. Then he said: > **""Men will emerge from the east — this man was as it were of them — their guidance thus. They recite the Quran but it does not pass their throats. They pass through religion as the arrow passes through the target and do not return to it.""** He placed his hand on his chest: > **""Their mark is shaving. They will keep emerging until the last of them emerges. When you see them, kill them.""** He said it three times: > **""The worst of creation and creatures.""** He said it three times."
"10409","In another version: > **""They will keep emerging until the last of them emerges with the Dajjal.""**"
"10410","Anas radiya Allahu anhu reported, though he did not hear it directly: > **""Among you are a people who worship and exert themselves until people admire them and they admire themselves. They pass through religion as the arrow passes through the target.""**"
"10411","Abdullah ibn Umar radiya Allahu anhuma reported: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""There will emerge from my ummah a people of evil deeds. They recite the Quran but it does not pass their throats. One of you will belittle his own deed beside theirs. They kill the people of Islam. When they emerge, kill them, then when they emerge, kill them, then when they emerge, kill them. Glad tidings to whoever kills them and to whoever they kill. Every time a generation of them rises, Allah the Mighty cuts it off.""** The Messenger of Allah ﷺ repeated that twenty times or more while I listened."
"10412","Uqbah ibn Amir radiya Allahu anhu reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""People from my ummah will emerge who drink the Quran as they drink milk.""**"
"10413","Uqbah ibn Amir radiya Allahu anhu reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Most of the hypocrites of my ummah are its reciters.""**"
"10414","Abdullah ibn Amr radiya Allahu anhu reported: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Most of the hypocrites of my ummah are its reciters.""**"
"10415","Ismah radiya Allahu anhu reported: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Most of the hypocrites of my ummah are its reciters.""**"
"10416","Abdullah ibn Amr radiya Allahu anhu reported: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""There will be among you a people reciting the Quran but it will not pass their throats. Every time a generation of them rises it is cut off.""** He mentioned it more than twenty times: > **""Until the last of them emerges with the Dajjal.""**"
"10417","From Abdullah ibn Amr radiya Allahu anhuma: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""People will emerge from the east reciting the Quran but it will not pass their throats. Every time a generation is cut off another rises, until the Dajjal is with their remnant.""**"
"10418","Amir ibn Wathilah radiya Allahu anhu reported: On the day of Hunayn a man with clipped or shaven head came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, You were not just. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: > **""Who will be just if I am not just?""** Attention turned from the man and he left. He said: > **""Where is the man?""** He was sought but not found. He said: > **""There will emerge in my ummah a people whose mark is like his. They pass through religion as the arrow passes through the target. One looks at its shaft and sees nothing, at its binding and sees nothing, at its head and sees nothing.""**"
"10419","Al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan al-Basri reported that al-Suraym met Abdullah ibn Khabbab radiya Allahu anhuma at al-Bidar, a village of Basrah, while he headed toward Ali radiya Allahu anhu at Kufah with wife, child and slave-girl. They said, Here is a man of the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ; shall we ask him about our state, affair and emergence. They said, Yes. They turned to him saying, Will you tell us whether you heard anything from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about us. He said, As for you specifically, no, but I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""After me there will be a people reciting the Quran but it will not pass their throats. They pass through religion then never return to it until the arrow returns to its notch. Glad tidings to whoever kills them and to whoever they kill. The worst slain under heaven's shade and earth's surface, dogs of Hellfire.""**"
"10420","Muslim ibn Abi Bakrah reported, when asked whether he heard anything about the Khawarij: I heard my father Abu Bakrah radiya Allahu anhu say from the Prophet ﷺ: > **""Soon there will emerge from my ummah peoples severe and sharp, their tongues fluent with the Quran but it will not pass their throats. When you see them, kill them, when you see them, kill them; rewarded is their killer.""**"
"10421","Jabir radiya Allahu anhu reported: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ divided the spoils of Hawazin, a man stood. The report continues until Umar stood and said, O Messenger of Allah, shall I rise and kill this hypocrite. He said: > **""Allah forbid; shall nations say Muhammad kills his companions.""**"
"10422","Abd al-Malik ibn Mulayl al-Sulayhi reported: I sat near the pulpit on Friday. Muhammad ibn Abi Hudhayfah emerged, mounted the pulpit, preached, then recited a surah of the Quran, being among the best reciters. Uqbah ibn Amir radiya Allahu anhu said, Allah and His Messenger spoke truth; I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Men will surely recite the Quran but it will not pass their throats. They pass through religion as the arrow passes through the target.""**"
"10423","Abu Sa'id al-Khudri radiya Allahu anhu reported: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""There will be successors after sixty who waste prayers and follow desires, and soon meet error. Then successors reciting the Quran but it will not pass their throats. The Quran is read by three: believer, hypocrite and sinner.""** Bashir asked al-Walid, Who are the three. He said, The hypocrite disbelieves in it, the sinner earns a living by it, and the believer believes in it."
"10424","Ali radiya Allahu anhu reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""In the last age a people will recite the Quran but it will not pass their throats. They pass out of Islam as the arrow passes through the target; fighting them is binding on every Muslim.""**"
"10425","Safwan ibn Muhriz from Jundab ibn Abdillah radiya Allahu anhu: He passed people reciting the Quran and said, Let them not deceive you; today they recite the Quran, tomorrow they clash with swords. Then he said, Bring me a group of Quran reciters, and let them be elders. He was brought Nafi' ibn al-Azraq, Mirdas ibn Bilal, and others with them, six or eight. When they entered Jundab said, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""The likeness of one who teaches people good and forgets himself is the lamp giving light to people while burning itself. Whoever shows off his deed to people, Allah exposes him. Know the first of you to putrefy when dead is the belly, so admit only the pure into the belly. Whoever can let not even a handful of blood stand between him and Paradise, let him do so.""**"
"10426","In another version: the people spoke of commanding good and forbidding evil while he listened silently, then said, I never saw like today a people more deserving of salvation, if they are truthful."
"10427","Abdullah ibn Mas'ud radiya Allahu anhu from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: > **""Soon a people will recite the Quran but it will not pass their throats. They drink it as they drink water but it will not pass their throats.""** Then he placed his hand on his throat and said: > **""It will not pass here.""**"
"10428","Ibn Abbas radiya Allahu anhuma reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Groups of my ummah will surely recite the Quran and pass out of Islam as the arrow passes through the target.""**"
"10429","Sa'id ibn Jumhan reported: I came to Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa radiya Allahu anhu when his sight was veiled, greeted him. He asked, Who are you. I said, Sa'id ibn Jumhan. He asked, What became of your father. I said, The Azariqah killed him. He said, May Allah curse the Azariqah, may Allah curse the Azariqah. Then he said, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Dogs of Hellfire.""** I asked, The Azariqah alone or all Khawarij. He said, All Khawarij. I said, The ruler wrongs people and does such-and-such. He took my hand, squeezed hard, then said, O Ibn Jumhan, hold to the great multitude. If the ruler hears from you, go to him in his house and tell him what you know; if he accepts, well, else leave him, for you know no more than he."
"10430","Talq ibn Ali radiya Allahu anhu reported: While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ he said to us: > **""Soon a people will come reciting the Quran but it will not pass their throats. They pass through religion as the arrow passes through the target. Glad tidings to whoever kills them and to whoever they kill.""** Then he turned to me and said: > **""They will emerge in your people's land, O Yamami, fighting between rivers.""** I said, At the cost of father and mother, there are no rivers there. He said: > **""There will be.""**"
"10431","Ibn Abbas radiya Allahu anhuma: the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""I will surely slay the Amalekites in a battalion.""** Jibril alayhi al-salam said to him, And Ali ibn Abi Talib."
"10432","Abu Umamah radiya Allahu anhu from the Prophet ﷺ about His saying, O believers take no intimates besides yourselves causing you no harm in corruption, loving your hardship, hatred shown from mouths and what breasts hide greater, We clarified signs if you reason, Al Imran 118. He said: > **""They are the Khawarij.""**"
"10433","Abdullah ibn Umayr al-Ashja'i radiya Allahu anhu reported: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: > **""If a rebel emerges against you while you are united under one man, seeking to split the staff of Muslims and divide their gathering, kill him.""**"
"10434","Muhammad ibn Surayh al-Ashja'i radiya Allahu anhu said: I narrate only what my ears heard and my heart retained from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, had I heard it but once or twice or thrice or four or five or six or seven times I would still narrate it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""When you are united and one comes to divide your gathering and split your staff, kill him, whoever among people he be.""**"
"10435","Buraydah radiya Allahu anhu reported: Abu Bakr radiya Allahu anhu said, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Kill the lone dissenter, whoever among people he be.""**"
"10436","Abu Ghalib reported: I was at Damascus in the time of Abd al-Malik when heads of the Khawarij were brought and set on poles. I came to see if any I knew was there, and Abu Umamah radiya Allahu anhu was beside them. I drew near, looked at the poles, and he said three times: > **""Dogs of Hellfire.""** > **""The worst slain under heaven's canopy, and those they kill the best slain under heaven's canopy.""** He said it three times, then wept. I asked, O Abu Umamah, what makes you weep. He said, They were upon our religion, then I remembered what they face tomorrow. I asked, Is this your opinion or something heard from the Messenger ﷺ. He said, Had I not heard it from the Messenger ﷺ but once or twice or thrice up to seven times, I would not narrate it to you. Have you not read in Al Imran, On the day faces whiten and faces blacken, Al Imran 106, to, As for those whose faces whiten, in Allah's mercy abiding, Al Imran 107. Then he said, Jews differed into seventy-one sects, seventy in Fire one in Paradise; Christians into seventy-two, seventy-one in Fire one in Paradise; this ummah differs into seventy-three, seventy-two in Fire one in Paradise. We asked, Describe them. He said, The great multitude."
"10437","Yahya ibn Yazid al-Huna'i reported: I was with al-Farazdaq in prison. Al-Farazdaq said, May Allah not save him from Malik ibn al-Mundhir ibn al-Jarud if I did not walk in Makkah meeting Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id al-Khudri radiya Allahu anhuma. I asked them, I am of the east; people emerge against us killing whoever says none is worthy of worship but Allah while sparing others. They told me — else may Allah not save me from Malik ibn al-Mundhir — We heard our close friend ﷺ say: > **""Whoever kills them has the reward of one martyr — or two martyrs — and whoever they kill has the reward of a martyr.""**"
"10438","Sa'd ibn Malik — meaning Ibn Abi Waqqas radiya Allahu anhu — heard the Prophet ﷺ mention Dhu al-Thudayyah found with the people of Nahrawan, saying: > **""A devil of the hollow, brought down by a man of Bajilah called al-Ashhab or Ibn al-Ashhab, a sign among an unjust people.""** Sufyan said Ammar al-Duhni when narrating said, A man of us of Bajilah brought him; I think from Duhn, called al-Ashhab or Ibn al-Ashhab."
"10439","Abu Sa'id radiya Allahu anhu reported: I attended the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Hunayn while he divided, then narrated until: > **""Their mark is a man whose hand is like a woman's breast, a lump of flesh with hairs rolling in it like a beast's forelock.""** Abu Sa'id said, I witnessed this from the Messenger ﷺ at Hunayn, and witnessed with Ali when he killed them at Nahrawan. Ali sought him and did not find him, then found him after beneath a wall of that description. Ali asked, Which of you knows this. A man said, We know him, this is Harqus, and his mother is here. Ali sent to his mother asking, Who is this. She said, I know not, O Commander of the Faithful, except I grazed sheep in Jahiliyyah at al-Rabadhah when something like darkness covered me, I conceived from it and bore him."
"10440","Yazid ibn Abi Salih that Abu al-Wadi' Abbad narrated: We headed to Kufah with Ali ibn Abi Talib radiya Allahu anhu, then mentioned the hadith of the defective-handed one. Ali said, By Allah I did not lie nor was lied to, thrice. Ali said: > **""My close friend ﷺ told me of three brothers of the jinn; this is the eldest, the second has a great host, the third has weakness in him.""**"
"10441","Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas: Ammar ibn Yasir radiya Allahu anhu said to Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas radiya Allahu anhu, Why do you not go out with Ali. Did you not hear the Messenger ﷺ say of him: > **""A people from my ummah will emerge passing through religion as the arrow passes through the target; Ali ibn Abi Talib kills them.""** He said it three times. He said, Yes by Allah I heard it, but I prefer seclusion until I find a sword cutting the disbeliever while sparing the believer."
"10442","Abdullah — meaning Ibn Mas'ud radiya Allahu anhu — reported: > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered fighting the oath-breakers, the deviators and the rebels.""**"
"10443","Muhannaf ibn Sulaym reported: We came to Abu Ayyub al-Ansari radiya Allahu anhu while he fed his horses at Sa'naba, and stayed. I said, O Abu Ayyub, you fought idolaters with the Messenger ﷺ then came to fight Muslims. He said, The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered me to fight three: oath-breakers, deviators and rebels. I fought the oath-breakers, fought the deviators, and will fight, Allah willing, the rebels at the palm-branches, roads and Nahrawans, though I know not where they are."
"10444","Ubaydullah ibn Iyad ibn Amr al-Qari: Abdullah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had came to Aishah radiya Allahu anha while we sat with her, returning from Iraq in the nights Ali ibn Abi Talib radiya Allahu anhu was killed. She asked, O Ibn Shaddad, will you tell me truth about what I ask. Tell me of those Ali killed. He said, Why would I not tell you truth. She said, Tell their story. He said, When Ali corresponded with Mu'awiyah radiya Allahu anhu and the two arbiters judged, eight thousand reciters rebelled, camped at Harura' by Kufah. They blamed him saying, You shed a shirt Allah clothed you, a name Allah named you, then arbitrated men in Allah's religion; no judgment but Allah's. When their blame and parting reached Ali, he ordered a caller that none enter the Commander of the Faithful but a bearer of the Quran. When the house filled with reciters he called for a great master copy, placed it before him, struck it with his hand saying: > **""O Mushaf, speak to the people.""** People called, O Commander of the Faithful, what you ask is but ink on paper speaking what we see; what do you want. He said, Those companions of yours who rebelled — between me and them is Allah's Book. Allah says concerning a woman and man, If you fear breach send an arbiter from his folk and an arbiter from her folk, Nisa 35. Is the sanctity of Muhammad's ummah ﷺ greater, or a man and woman. They blamed that when writing Mu'awiyah he wrote Ali ibn Abi Talib. Suhayl ibn Amr once came; the Messenger ﷺ wrote: > **""In the name of Allah, the Merciful, the Compassionate.""** He said, Write not that. He asked: > **""How shall we write?""** Suhayl said, Write, In Your name O Allah. The Messenger ﷺ said: > **""Write, Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.""** He said, Had I known you Allah's Messenger I would not oppose you. So he wrote: > **""This is what Muhammad ibn Abdillah conciliated Quraysh upon.""** Allah says in His Book, You have in Allah's Messenger a fine example for whoever hopes in Allah and the Last Day, Ahzab 21. He sent Abdullah ibn Abbas radiya Allahu anhuma to them; I went with him until amid their camp. Ibn al-Kawwa' stood preaching, O bearers of the Quran, this is Abdullah ibn Abbas; whoever knows him not, know him; I know him from Allah's Book, of those revealed about, A disputatious people. Return him to his master and do not debate Allah's Book with him. Their preachers rose saying, By Allah we shall debate the Book with him; if he brings truth we know, we follow; if false, we refute with falsehood and return him to his master. They debated Abdullah ibn Abbas the Book three days; four thousand repented, including Ibn al-Kawwa', until Ali brought them into Kufah. Ali sent to the rest: Our affair and people's you have seen; stand where you will on condition between us you shed no unlawful blood, cut no road, wrong no covenant; if you do, we declare war openly: Allah loves not traitors. Aishah asked, O Ibn Shaddad, so he killed them. He said, By Allah he sent none until they cut roads, shed blood, violated covenant. She said, By Allah. He said, By Allah besides whom none is worthy of worship, so it was. She asked twice about what Iraqis relate, Dhu al-Thudayyah. He said, I saw him, stood with Ali over him among slain; he called people asking: > **""Do you know this?""** Most who came said, I saw him praying in such-and-such mosque, with no firm identification but that. She asked, What did Ali say standing over him as Iraqis claim. He said, I heard him say, Allah and His Messenger spoke truth. She asked, Did you see him say else. He said, O Allah, no. She said, Yes, Allah and His Messenger spoke truth; mercy upon Ali, it was his speech never seeing anything marvelous but saying, Allah and His Messenger spoke truth, while Iraqis go lying upon him and adding to report."
"10445","Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Abu Wa'il: I asked him about those Ali killed. In what did they part from him, deem him lawful, call them, deem their blood lawful. He said, When slaughter intensified among Syrians at Siffin, he and companions clung to a hill. Amr ibn al-As said, Send him the Mushaf; by Allah we shall not turn it back. A man came bearing it calling, Between us and you is Allah's Book, Have you not seen those given a portion of the Book, Al Imran 23, to the verse. Ali said, Yes, between us and you is Allah's Book; I am worthier of it than you. Then came the Khawarij, then called Qurra', swords on shoulders, saying, O Commander of the Faithful, shall we not march to those until Allah judges between us. Sahl ibn Hunayf rose saying, O people, accuse yourselves. We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Hudaybiyah; had we seen fighting we would fight, in the truce between the Messenger ﷺ and idolaters. Umar ibn al-Khattab came saying, O Messenger of Allah, are we not upon truth and they upon falsehood. He said: > **""Yes.""** He said, Are not our slain in Paradise and theirs in Fire. He said: > **""Yes.""** He said, Why concede lowliness in religion and return before Allah judges between us. He said: > **""O son of al-Khattab, I am Allah's Messenger and He will never forsake me.""** Umar went unpatiently in anger to Abu Bakr asking, O Abu Bakr, are we not upon truth and they upon falsehood. He said, Yes. Are not our slain in Paradise and theirs in Fire. He said, Yes. Why concede lowliness in religion before Allah judges between us. He said, O son of al-Khattab, he is Allah's Messenger and Allah will never forsake him. Then the Quran of victory descended upon Muhammad; he sent to Umar and recited. He asked, O Messenger of Allah, is it victory. He said: > **""Yes.""** His soul settled and he returned, people returned. Then they exited at Harura', that band of Khawarij over ten thousand. Ali sent imploring them by Allah; they refused. Sa'sa'ah ibn Sawhan came imploring, saying, Why fight your caliph. They said, Fear of fitnah. He said, Hasten not this year's misguidance fearing next year's fitnah. They returned saying, We march as we came; if Ali accepts the case we fight as at Siffin, if he breaks we fight with him. They marched to Nahrawan. A faction split raiding people by night. Their companions said, Woe, not for this did we part from Ali. When it reached Ali he preached asking, What deem you, march to Syrians or return to those left among your offspring. They said, Return. He mentioned their affair, narrating about them what the Messenger ﷺ said: > **""A sect emerges at people's division; the nearer to truth of the two parties kills them. Their mark is a man among them whose hand is like a woman's breast.""** They marched meeting at Nahrawan, fighting fiercely; Ali's cavalry would not stand. Ali said, O people, if you fight for me, by Allah I have no reward for you; if for Allah, let not this be your conduct. People charged together; cavalry scattered from them fallen on faces. Ali rose saying, Seek the man among them. People sought but found him not, until some said, Ibn Abi Talib deceived us of our brothers till we killed them. Ali's eye teared; he called his mount, rode to a hollow with slain piled, dragged them by legs till found the man beneath. They told him; Ali said, Allah is Greatest. He rejoiced, people rejoiced and returned. Ali said, I campaign not this year. He returned to Kufah, was killed mercy upon him; al-Hasan succeeded upon his father's conduct, then sent allegiance to Mu'awiyah."
"10446","Kulayb ibn Shihab reported: I sat with Ali radiya Allahu anhu while busy with people's affairs. A travel-clad man came saying, O Commander of the Faithful, but Ali remained occupied. Kulayb asked, What is your matter. He said, I performed Hajj or Umrah, passed Aishah radiya Allahu anha who asked, Who are those who rebelled toward you called Haruriyyah. I said, From a place called Harura', hence named. She said, Glad tidings to whoever witnesses their destruction; by Allah, if Ibn Abi Talib wished he could tell you their report. So I came asking. When Ali finished he asked, Where is the seeker of leave. He stood recounting as before. Ali thrice proclaimed Allah's greatness then said, I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with none but Aishah present, and he said to me: > **""O Ali, how will you be with a people emerging in such-and-such place.""** motioning east with his hand: > **""They recite the Quran but it will not pass their throats — or collarbones. They pass out of Islam as the arrow passes through the target. Among them a defective-handed man whose hand is like an Abyssinian woman's breast.""** Then he adjured those present whether he had told them he was among them; they said yes; whether they went seeking and dragged him as described; then said thrice, Allah and His Messenger spoke truth."
"10447","Aishah radiya Allahu anha mentioned the Khawarij asking who killed them — the people of the river. They said, Ali. She said, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""The best of my ummah kill them, and they are the worst of my ummah.""**"
"10448","Aishah radiya Allahu anha asked, Who killed Dhu al-Thudayyah, Ali ibn Abi Talib radiya Allahu anhu. They said, Yes. She said, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""A people will emerge reciting the Quran but it will not pass their throats. They pass through religion as the arrow passes through the target. Their mark is a defective-handed man.""**"
"10449","Ali radiya Allahu anhu said, Those of knowledge from the family of Muhammad and Aishah bint Abi Bakr radiya Allahu anha know that the companions of Dhu al-Thudayyah are cursed upon the tongue of the unlettered Prophet ﷺ; in another version, the people of Nahrawan."
"10450","Ibn Abbas radiya Allahu anhuma reported: When Haruriyyah seceded apart, I told Ali radiya Allahu anhu, O Commander of the Faithful, delay prayer that I may go speak to them. He said, I fear them for you. I said, No, Allah willing. I wore my best Yamani garments, entered at midday rest upon a people never seen more striving, hands like camel knees, faces marked from prostration. They welcomed, O Ibn Abbas, what brings you. I said, I come to speak of the Companions of the Messenger ﷺ; revelation descended and they know its interpretation. Some said, Speak not to him; others said, We shall speak. I asked, What do you blame upon the cousin of the Messenger ﷺ, his son-in-law, first believer, with the Companions with him. They said, Three things. I asked, What. They said, First he arbitrated men in Allah's religion while Allah says, Judgment is but Allah's, An'am 57. I asked, What else. They said, He fought but took no captives nor spoils; if disbelievers their wealth was lawful, if believers their blood unlawful. I asked, What else. They said, He erased himself from Commander of the Faithful; if not their commander then commander of disbelievers. I said, If I recite decisive Book and narrate your Prophet's Sunnah ﷺ undeniable, will you return. They said, Yes. I said, As for arbitrating men, Allah says, O believers kill no game in pilgrim sanctity, Ma'idah 95, to, judged by two just men among you, Ma'idah 95, and concerning spouses, If you fear breach send an arbiter from his folk and an arbiter from hers, Nisa 35. I adjure you by Allah, is men's judgment in blood, lives and reconciliation worthier, or concerning a rabbit worth quarter dirham. They said, O Allah, in sparing blood and reconciliation. I said, Are you out of this. They said, O Allah, yes. As for fighting without captives or spoils, would you enslave your mother or deem lawful from her what from others; you have disbelieved. If you claim she is not your mother you disbelieved and exited Islam; Allah says, The Prophet is nearer to believers than themselves and his wives their mothers, Ahzab 6. You waver between two misguidances; choose. Are you out of this. They said, O Allah, yes. As for erasing Commander of the Faithful, the Messenger ﷺ at Hudaybiyah called Quraysh to write a document, saying: > **""Write: This is what Muhammad the Messenger of Allah conciliated upon.""** They said, By Allah had we known you Allah's Messenger we would not bar you nor fight you; write Muhammad ibn Abdillah. He said: > **""By Allah I am Allah's Messenger though you belie me. Write, O Ali: Muhammad ibn Abdillah.""** The Messenger ﷺ was better than Ali. Are you out of this. They said, O Allah, yes. Twenty thousand returned; four thousand remained and were killed."
"10451","Jundab radiya Allahu anhu reported: When the Khawarij parted from Ali, he went seeking them and we with him, reaching their camp with a hum like bees from Quran recital, men of calloused knees and hooded cloaks. Awe entered me; I withdrew, planted my spear, dismounted, laid cap and coat, held my horse's rein, praying toward my spear: O Allah, if fighting them is obedience permit me, if disobedience show me innocence. Then Ali ibn Abi Talib came on the Messenger's mule ﷺ; abreast he said, Seek Allah's refuge from evil of doubt, O Jundab. I hastened; he dismounted praying when a rider approached asking, O Commander of the Faithful, have you need regarding the people. What. They crossed the river. He said, They did not cross. I said, Glory be to Allah. Another swifter came repeating; I said, Allah is Greatest. Ali said, They did not cross. A third galloping came repeating; he said, They did not cross nor shall, but shall be killed short of it, a covenant from Allah and His Messenger. I said, Allah is Greatest. I held his stirrup; he mounted his horse; I donned coat, hung bow, marching beside. He told me, O Jundab, I shall send a man reciting the Mushaf calling to Allah's Book and his Prophet's Sunnah ﷺ, and he shall not return facing us until showered with arrows. O Jundab, not ten of us shall be killed nor ten of them spared. We reached them unmoved in camp. Ali arrayed companions, walked the line twice asking, Who takes this Mushaf to them calling to Allah's Book and his Prophet's Sunnah, to be killed with Paradise. None answered but a youth of Banu Amir ibn Sa'sa'ah. Seeing his youth Ali said, Return to your post. He called second, third; only the youth emerged. Ali said, Take. He took; Ali said, You shall be killed and not return facing us until showered with arrows. The youth went; within hearing they rose wounding him before return; a man shot; he turned facing us and sat. Ali said, Upon the people. Jundab said, With this hand I killed eight before Zuhr after my earlier awe; not ten of us killed nor ten of them spared, as he said."
"10452","Abu Ja'far al-Farra', freedman of Ali, reported: I witnessed with Ali at the river. When finished killing them he said, Seek the defective-handed. They sought but found him not, and he ordered a reed placed on each slain. They found him in a hollow in stagnant water, a black man of foul odor, in place of his hand like a breast with hairs. When he saw him he said, Allah and His Messenger spoke truth. He heard one of his two sons — al-Hasan or al-Husayn — say, Praise to Allah who relieved Muhammad's ummah ﷺ of this band. Ali said, Had but three of Muhammad's ummah ﷺ remained, one would be upon their view; they are in men's loins and women's wombs."
"10453","Abd al-Rahman ibn Udays al-Balawi radiya Allahu anhu reported: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: > **""People will emerge passing through religion as the arrow passes through the target. They shall be killed at Mount Lebanon — or Mount Khalil.""** Ibn Lahi'ah said, Ibn Udays was killed at Mount Lebanon or Mount Khalil."
"10454","Kathir ibn Namir reported: I entered Kufah mosque Friday evening while Ali preached; they stood in mosque corners chanting arbitration. He gestured with his hand then said, A word of truth sought for falsehood. I await Allah's judgment among you; I judge you by Allah's Book and His Messenger's Sunnah ﷺ, divide equally, bar you not from this mosque praying while your hands are with ours, and fight you not until you fight us."
"10455","Ibn Umar radiya Allahu anhuma: the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""O son of Umm Abd, do you know Allah's ruling on rebels of this ummah?""** He said, Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: > **""Their wounded are not finished, their captive not killed, their fugitive not pursued, their spoils not sought.""**"
"10456","Abu al-Tufayl reported that a boy was born in the Messenger's time ﷺ; brought to the Prophet ﷺ, he took his forehead skin praying blessing, and a hair grew like a horse's forelock. The boy grew; in Khawarij times he loved them, and the hair fell from his forehead. His father bound and confined him fearing joining them. They entered admonishing, Did you not see blessing of the Messenger's supplication ﷺ fall from your forehead. They persisted till he renounced their view; Allah restored the hair after, and he repented."
"10457","Yazid ibn al-Asamm reported: I went out with al-Hasan radiya Allahu anhu while a slave-girl scraped henna from his nails. A bundle of letters came. He said, O girl, bring the basin; pour water. He cast the letters in water, opening none nor looking. I asked, O Abu Muhammad, from whom. He said, From Iraqis, a people returning to no truth nor falling short of falsehood. I fear them not for myself, but fear them for him, pointing to al-Husayn."
"10458","Abu Sa'id al-Khudri radiya Allahu anhu reported: We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said: > **""Among you is one who fights for interpretation of the Quran as I fought for its revelation.""**"
"10459","Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' radiya Allahu anhu reported: I asked the Prophet ﷺ, Is it partisanship for a man to love his people. He said: > **""No, but partisanship is for a man to aid his people in wrongdoing.""**"
"10460","Ibn Abbas radiya Allahu anhuma from the Prophet ﷺ: > **""Whoever is killed defending his right is a martyr.""**"
"10461","Abu Bakr ibn Hafs: Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas radiya Allahu anhu said, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Fine is the death for a man to die for his right.""**"
"10462","Husayn ibn Ali radiya Allahu anhuma reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever is killed for his property is a martyr.""**"
"10463","Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas radiya Allahu anhu reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever is killed for his property is a martyr.""**"
"10464","Jabir ibn Abdillah radiya Allahu anhuma reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever is killed for his property is a martyr.""**"
"10465","Abdullah — meaning Ibn Mas'ud radiya Allahu anhu — reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever is killed for his property is a martyr.""**"
"10466","Anas radiya Allahu anhu from the Prophet ﷺ: > **""The slain for his property is a martyr.""**"
"10467","Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr radiya Allahu anhuma and Abdullah ibn Kurayz: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever is killed for his property is a martyr.""**"
"10468","Ibn Abbas radiya Allahu anhuma: the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""The slain for his property is a martyr, the slain for his family is a martyr, the slain for himself is a martyr.""**"
"10469","Shaddad ibn Aws radiya Allahu anhu reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever wrongfully takes a span of land is collared with seven earths, and whoever is killed for his property is a martyr.""**"
"10470","Quhayd ibn Mutarrif al-Ghifari radiya Allahu anhu: a questioner asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, If an aggressor attacks me. He ordered him to forbid him thrice. He asked, If he refuses. He ordered fighting him. He asked, How fare we. He said: > **""If he kills you, you are in Paradise, and if you kill him, he is in the Fire.""**"
"10471","Ubadah ibn al-Samit radiya Allahu anhu: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The house is sanctuary; whoever enters your sanctuary against you, kill him.""**"
